  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing Trafficking in Persons and Related Risks in the Ukraine Emergency Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will leverage the Organization&apos;s in-country pre-war work as well as global-level experience for countering trafficking in persons (TiP) in crisis. IOM will be assisting primarily TiP survivors as well as individuals who are crisis-affected and at high risk of human trafficking. Other activities will be focused on the typical counter-trafficking (CT) pillars but will be adapted to the new reality. The inevitable part of the project activities will be focused on integration of CT indicators into the humanitarian response of a variety of stakeholders operating in Ukraine. Both the capacity building activities as well as data collection, will be based on IOM&apos;s expertise within the global project &quot;Addressing Human Trafficking in Emergency Contexts&quot;, and will adapt the good practices to be relevant to the current Ukrainian contexts.</narrative>
  </description>
